{"c": null, "r": "I'm designing a Bank class where each instance maintains its own accounts dictionary initialized in __init__ to prevent shared state across instances. I'm also defining a custom InsufficientFunds exception and implementing validation checks like ensuring amounts are positive integers.

For the module-level API, I'm creating a default_bank singleton and exposing the core operations—open_account, deposit, withdraw, balance, transfer—as functions that delegate to it. The transfer method validates the same-account constraint before checking if accounts exist, and all methods raise KeyError for unknown names.
", "t": [["write_file", "{"path":"D:\\Projects\\local_ai\\strata-lab\\runs\\work\\hermes\\bank-1794053343\\bank.py","content":"\"\"\"Account helpers. Balances are integer cents.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass InsufficientFunds(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a withdrawal or transfer exceeds the source balance.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _check_amount(amount):\n    if amount <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"amount must be positive, got {!r}\".format(amount))\n\n\nclass Bank:\n    \"\"\"A set of named accounts holding integer-cent balances.\n\n    Each Bank owns its own accounts; two instances never share them.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._accounts = {}\n\n    def open_account(self, name, initial=0):\n        if name in self._accounts:\n            raise ValueError(\"account exists: \" + name)\n        if initial < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"initial must be >= 0, got {!r}\".format(initial))\n        self._accounts[name] = initial\n\n    def deposit(self, name, amount):\n        _check_amount(amount)\n        self._accounts[name] += amount\n\n    def withdraw(self, name, amount):\n        _check_amount(amount)\n        current = self._accounts[name]\n        if current < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"balance for {!r} is {}, cannot withdraw {}\".format(name, current, amount))\n        self._accounts[name] = current - amount\n\n    def balance(self, name):\n        return self._accounts[name]\n\n    def transfer(self, src, dst, amount):\n        _check_amount(amount)\n        if src == dst:\n            raise ValueError(\"cannot transfer to the same account: \" + src)\n        src_balance = self._accounts[src]\n        dst_balance = self._accounts[dst]\n        if src_balance < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"balance for {!r} is {}, cannot transfer {}\".format(src, src_balance, amount))\n        self._accounts[src] = src_balance - amount\n        self._accounts[dst] = dst_balance + amount\n\n\ndefault_bank = Bank()\n\n\ndef open_account(name, initial=0):\n    return default_bank.open_account(name, initial)\n\n\ndef deposit(name, amount):\n    return default_bank.deposit(name, amount)\n\n\ndef withdraw(name, amount):\n    return default_bank.withdraw(name, amount)\n\n\ndef balance(name):\n    return default_bank.balance(name)\n\n\ndef transfer(src, dst, amount):\n    return default_bank.transfer(src, dst, amount)\n"}"]]}

